            <ArticleTitle>3D reconstruction from contrast coronary angiography in magnetic percutaneous coronary intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>532-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.22519</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The magnetic navigation system allows precision wire-tip control that is guided by computer generated 3D models based on fluoroscopic images. These images can be post-processed and the information used to facilitate steering of wires in difficult anatomy. This report illustrates two of these reconstruction software packages in a challenging saphenous vein graft case.</AbstractText>
